\import{base-macros}

\p{Under \code{\verb~|directrules~}, first named \code{\verb~|m3a~}, a recursor rule of the plain form is one application of the minor premise, and induction hypotheses that nothing reads are not built: reachability 21.9 to 20.7 G instructions, Init and Std -1 \%; 400 random applications are tested against the generic reduction. The same publication brought \code{\verb~|k2~}, derived rule trees for hot definitions that have no case tree. Its gates were green and it gains on input that mostly evaluates (reachability 3.08 and 3.09 s to 2.47 and 2.66 s CPU on top of \code{\verb~|code,casetrees~}, two runs each on a loaded host). But its derivation variables are free variables of a reserved type and not the dedicated value kind that the design asks for, so it stays off until that is decided and reviewed. \code{\verb~|directrules~} joined the default set at the integration of wave 6.}

\p{Detail: \src{rlvm-machine/SWITCHES.md}, \src{rlvm-machine/NOTES-M3.md}. Commit \commit{468d682}. Session: [machine speed and pipeline](ses-CVTE).}
